<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hammudid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1016">1016</a>–1058</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Hammudids, Banu Hammud</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hammudids were a Berber-backed Arab dynasty of Idrisid descent that briefly held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> between 1016 and 1027 during the civil war that broke up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. They then ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of Málaga and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeciras">Algeciras</a>, claiming the caliphal title, and led an alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> taifas against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> until the Zirids of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> took Málaga in 1057.</p></div>
